==Changelog - September 16th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Summer Sweep Up - Pet Changes'''

* Pets will now follow you into The Gauntlet, Corrupted Gauntlet and Impetuous Impulses, meaning you won't need to bank them before entering and they will be visibly following you inside.
* For other minigames ''except Temple Trekking'', you'll now be able to enter them without needing to bank your pet, if you have one following you. However, pets will be invisible once inside the minigame, still saving you the trouble of banking them.
** Our initial intent was to allow pets to fully follow you into various other minigames, but unfortunately we had technical limitations for a number of these, where new NPCs wandering around would mean the minigame would break. We've managed to crack the Gauntlet and Impetuous Impulses, but other instances have had to settle for at least allowing you access without needing to bank your pet.
** Temple Trekking is excluded from this list since you already have an NPC following in that minigame, so you'll still need to bank your pet to be able to enter there.
* You'll now be able to enter the Fossil Island's Underwater area without needing to bank the pet following you, but it will be invisible.
** We'll look to apply this to Tortugan Island's Underwater area as well in a future update.
* Pets will now respawn with you on death and will keep on following you.

Note that for all the above minigame and underwater related pet changes:

* Your pet needs to be in a summoned status before entering, meaning you cannot take an Inventory item pet into the minigames.
* Once you leave the underwater area and minigames that your pet is invisible, your pet will go back to visibly following you.
* If you die within the minigame or drown in the Fossil Island's Underwater area, pets will be kept in a status of following you.
* These changes apply to all pets except the list of "[https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Pet#Other_(Generic) Other (Generic)]": Dogs, cats, Broav, Pet fish, Hellcat, Pet rock, Toy cat, Humphrey Dumphrey, Spooky chair, Mayor of Catherby, and Archibald.

<u>An additional Summer Sweep Up Tweak</u>

* Reduced the amount of energy potions dropped from Goblins, Banshees and Crawling Hands. Players should still receive a useful amount, but these should no longer dominate loot tables or feel overly abundant.

'''Tweaks for Our Canine Companions'''

* Fixed a bug where you couldn't see the location of locked puppies in the adoption interface if you already owned a dog.
* The following food can no longer be fed to dogs:
** Onions sacks
** Poison Karambwan
** Easter egg
** Green, Plain, Red, Black, Gold and Rune satchels

'''Z-buffer Related Fixes'''

* Fixed clipping issues for:
** Drops on the floor of Cerberus' lair
** Drops on a few tiles in the Tormented Demon dungeon
