'''Other Changes'''

* Fixed an issue where certain Mortimer Partner Slayer scenarios could lock players out from Slayer. Players affected by this issue should now be able to get Slayer tasks again.
* In Chambers of Xeric, the range, magic and melee thralls now respectively change the colours of the Jewelled crabs upon attacking.
** The Ghost thrall dealing magic damage changes the colour of the crab to blue.
** The Skeleton thrall dealing ranged damage changes to the colour of the crab to green.
** The Zombie thrall dealing melee damage changes the colour of the crab to red.
* Players using a Medallion of the Deep to breathe underwater are now permitted to equip capes and helms down there, since they are not using those slots for diving gear.
* When sorting salvage, players who are eligible to receive clue boxes can now receive those, instead of just clues. This resolves the issue whereby a player who already had a clue could not receive another one of that tier from their salvage even if they had unlocked clue boxes.
* Making Guthix Balance potions now uses the make-x interface.
* Resolved an issue where the 'Play' option of the Enchanted Lyre couldn't be used without completing the Hard and Elite Fremennik Diary.
* Fixed a bug where completing Achievement Diary tasks didn't show the relevant messaging in the chatbox if a player hasn't relogged at least once after finishing Tutorial Island.
* Adjusted various inventory icons:
** Sunlight and Moonlight moth mixes now have different inventory icons and no longer share the same one as Sapphire Glacialis.
** The inventory icons of all butterfly and moth mixes have been adjusted to distinguish them from their non-mix variants.
** Tweaked the inventory icons for cooked Hunter meat and cooked Halibut to better display that they are the cooked variants.
** Increased the size of the Crystal Legs inventory icons so that they'd be more user-friendly.
* Mausoleum-Repair bridge entry is no longer blank in the Construction skill guide.
* Some more item names have had their capitalisation adjusted, including schematics, more Scythe of Vitur variants, Perilous Moons equipment and more books.
* Fixed a typo at the second plaque in Ruins of Ullek.
* Some text has been corrected for interacting with fur pouches.

