==Checking In: Jagex Launcher on Mac==
In case you've missed [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/a=13/checking-in-jagex-launcher-on-mac?oldschool=1 our blog] yesterday, we want to check in with you regarding Jagex Launcher on Mac.

We’ve been working away on an Apple Silicon native version of the Jagex Launcher, with a provisional release window within the next two months.

This means we’ll be well ahead of the compatibility for Intel-based applications ending, which is due to take place with macOS 28 in 2027. However, with MacOS 27 having released yesterday, there will be a temporary step up until our native Launcher version releases that we want you to be aware of.

Our current Launcher is an Intel-based application which relies on Rosetta for compatibility. '''Rosetta is not installed by default on macOS 27''', so if you upgrade to this OS, the launcher may fail to open the first time you boot it.

If that happens, you’ll immediately see a one-time prompt to install Rosetta; you’ll need to be online, accept the install and may need to re-enter your macOS credentials. After that, everything should work normally with no further disruptions.

====Jagex Launcher Minimum Spec====
We also want to let you know about a change to the minimum spec for the Jagex Launcher. We avoid these changes as much as we can, but this key change will mean we can better support the majority of our Mac players.

For Mac users, minimum spec will move from macOS Big Sur (macOS 11) up to macOS Monterey (macOS 12). So, if you're still on macOS 11 or earlier, you'll need to update your OS to keep using the Launcher once this update goes live.

The minimum spec stays at Windows 10 for Windows players. That said, if you're on Windows 7 or 8, it's worth knowing these are already unsupported - so we can't promise the Launcher will keep working on them once the update rolls out.

==Jagex Launcher for Linux Beta==
[[File:Summer Sweep-Up Pet Improvements & More (6).gif|600px|center]]

In case you missed it, back in July we released the Jagex Launcher for Linux beta! Through this Launcher, you can login to your Jagex Account securely and access RuneLite to play OSRS on Linux.

You can read up on it in our launch blog, [https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/jagex-launcher-for-linux-beta-out-now?oldschool=1 here].

Since then, we've been working away on updates and fixes, with five updates under our belts that have addressed key feedback we've received from you, including:

* Adding in-app persisted log in
* Removing the need for you to install Fuse 2 to launch the application
* Improved automatic update checks from being too aggressive
* Allowed you to choose if the Launcher minimises on game launch
* Given you the ability to configure RuneLite from the App itself
* And many more under the hood tweaks to improve the experience!

We want to say a massive thank you for your support and feedback so far, your reports have really helped us identify bugs and make improvements.

In the bottom right of the launcher, there’s a quick logout style satisfaction rating you can provide. Please do let us know what you think.

If you encounter any bugs or issues, drop a report via our Official Discord server, through the [https://osrs.game/Linux-Launcher-Beta-Feedback #Linux-Launcher] channel. Our team will be logging any reports in here for our technical folks, and we may reach out from time to time for more information.

Thank you to all our Linux players for your continued support. We hope you enjoy a more direct route to getting onto the grind.

==Player Support and Anti-Cheating Statistics==
Welcome back to our monthly snapshot of Player Support and Anti-Cheating activity - your behind-the-scenes look at all the hard work going into keeping Gielinor fair and fun for everyone.

Each month, we share key stats from our Player Support and Anti-Cheating teams so you can see exactly what’s been happening behind the curtain. From how quickly we’re responding to your queries, to the number of bots and rule breakers taken down, here’s the latest data for August 2026:

